 if part == \"*\": values.update(range(min,max+1)); continue\n       if \"/\" in part:\n          base, step_text = part.split(\"/\", 1)\n          if step_text==\"\" or not step_text.isdigit(): invalid\n          Important `isdigit` accepts unicode digits; int works perhaps. Use fullmatch `[0-9]+`.\n          step=int\n          if step ==0 invalid\n          if base == \"*\": start=min,end=max\n          else:\n             parse_range(base,min,max)\n             if \"/\" in base? split only once and base could contain slash; range parser rejects.\n          values.update(range(start,end+1,step))\n       elif \"-\" in part:\n          start,end=_parse_range\n          values.update(range)\n       elif re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9]+\", part):\n          value=int; range\n       else invalid.\n    if no values impossible? Every part valid. Return frozenset.\nRange parse:\nparts=base.split(\"-\")\nif len !=2 invalid\neach digits\nrange bounds\nif start>end invalid\nCould number \"01\" accepted. likely yes. \"N\" decimal. Step \"00\" gives 0 invalid.\nCould plus signs no.\nCould \"1-2/3\" okay.\n\"1/2\" base no range and not star => invalid.\n\"*/2/3\" step_text not digits -> invalid.\nComma list \"*\" plus number okay.\n\"restricted = text != \"*\" exact. Important if `*,1`: restricted. Field exact '*' false.\nCould perhaps reject `*,1`? No.\n\nExpression field splitting: `expression.split()` gives tokens and ignores multiple whitespace. Exactly len5. If expression includes newline, split whitespace accepted. That's fine.\nPotential commas with spaces split into extra field -> invalid.\nRaise ValueError informative.\n\nAfter validation:\nif not isinstance(after, datetime): maybe TypeError natural? Signature. Could raise TypeError(\"after must be a datetime\"). User says datetimes naive. We can reject aware:\nif after.tzinfo is not None or after.utcoffset() is not None: raise ValueError(\"after must be timezone-naive\")\n`utcoffset()` can error custom tz, but not needed.\n`af