ts:\nUse subprocess [sys.executable,\"-m\",\"cronlite\",expr,\"--after\",\"2024-01-01T00:00\",\"--count\",\"3\"], cwd project root? Test file current when invoked root. But robust set cwd Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]. capture.\nassert return0 stdout exact:\nexpr \"* * * * *\" => 00:01,00:02,00:03.\nInvalid expression return2 stderr nonempty stdout empty.\nInvalid after return2.\nMaybe count invalid.\nTest no fire return2 message.\nCould test default after? Hard nondeterministic but format. Not necessary.\nUse no external.\n\nREADME:\n# cronlite\nInstall/use from root.\nAPI example.\nCLI.\nSyntax details DOM DOW and errors.\n8 years.\nShort.\n\nNeed write all maybe parallel Write? write files can run parallel since independent. Use multi_tool parallel of write. Need content exact. Let's formulate core carefully.\n\nPotential concern datetime horizon. Let's make helper:\ndef _deadline(after):\n try:\n   return after.replace(year=after.year+8)\n except ValueError:\n   try return after.replace(year=after.year+8, day=28)\n   except ValueError: return datetime.max\n except OverflowError? replace year 10000 raises ValueError likely. datetime.replace raises ValueError year 10000. So:\ndef _add_years(value, years):\n try: return value.replace(year=value.year+years)\n except ValueError:\n    try:return value.replace(year=value.year+years, day=28)\n    except ValueError:return datetime.max\nBut if date other than Feb29 and year overflow, first ValueError due year, second still year overflow. If Feb29 and year valid, first due day, second day 28. Good. But first exception could be due year only. fine.\nNeed candidate &lt;= deadline.\nIf after = 9991-12-31 23:59, deadline=9999-12-31; start overflow? datetime max only 9999, start 10000 invalid. There are likely cron candidates earlier? Strict after at 23:59 max second date beyond representable. No future representable; ValueError okay.\n\nStart:\ntry:\n  start=truncated+timedelta(minutes=1)\nexcept OverflowError:\n raise ValueError(\"no run found within 8 years\")\nIf after 9999-12-31 23:58:30, start=23:59, candidate could match same minute and is after after actual (23:58:30). Return 23:59. Good. after 23:59:30 => start overflow because truncated 23:59 +1 => year10000, but no minute candidate strictly after actual except 00:00 next day unrepresentable. error.\nIf after 23:59:00 exactly, no future minute representable. error.\n\nDeadline based after exact seconds; candidate <=. Fine.\n\nSearch date ordinal and candidate. `_candidate_for_date`:\nif day == start_date:\n  for hour...\n    for minute...\n      candidate=datetime.combine(day,time(hour,minute))\n      if candidate >= start: return\nelse:\n  return datetime.combine(day,time(min(hours),min(minutes)))\nNo time object name conflict with module. import `time as dt_time` from datetime.\nHours/minutes always nonempty. Parse \"*,1\" all.\n\nMonth/date values sets.\n\nParsing field exact wildcard:\ndef _parse_field(text,...):\n  restricted = text != \"*\"\nThis treats text `\"*\"` only. Need if text contains e.g. `*,1`, star part values all. fine.\nCould a field comma list only \"*\" duplicates e.g. `*,*` restricted true but all values. valid syntactically. Fine.\n\nRegex compiled `_DIGITS = re.compile(r\"[0-9]+\\Z\")` use fullmatch.\n`_parse_number` helper. Number leading zeros accepted. `int`.\nRange:\ndef _parse_range(part, min,max,field):\n pieces=part.split(\"-\")\n if len !=2 or empty etc invalid\n start parse...\n if out bounds invalid\n if end < start invalid\n return.\nFor step base:\nif base == \"*\" start min/end max\nelse:\n  if \"-\" not in base: invalid (single/step unsupported)\n  parse range.\nWhat about base `\"1\"` in \"1/2\": requirement only A-B/S, so invalid. Good.\n`*/2` okay.\nCould range step `1-59/2`.\n\"*/S\" starts field lowest and includes until max. yes.\n\nField names for errors.\n\nExpression:\nparts=expression.split()\nif len !=5.\nNo check isinstance expression str; if not, AttributeError. Signature